(4) VERDICTS
  V1  THE DERIVED EXPONENT: the CDF/mass-distribution exponent -n enters the
      r^-gamma -> n inversion; gamma = (2+n)/n as committed, n = 2/(gamma-1).
      The phantom identity pins it: dM_ph/dg ~ g^-2 EXACTLY (measured slope -2.000000 on the committed M_ph = M_b r/r_M + deep law), i.e. the mass-
      distribution carries -n at n = 2, not -(n+1) = -3.  The PDF exponent
      n(1+u)^-(n+1) belongs to the kernel's ratio-density and NEVER enters the
      profile-slope inversion (it would give gamma(2) = 5/3, dead at z = -16.7).
      THE OFF-BY-ONE IS RESOLVED IN FAVOR OF THE COMMITTED MASS-DISTRIBUTION
      EXPONENT -n: the suspicion (H060's flagged note) is adjudicated AWAY.
  V2  THE THREE-MEASUREMENT CONSISTENCY:  chi2_A = 5.0 vs chi2_B = 288.6 vs chi2_C = 640.8.
      Convention A returns the phantom point EXACTLY (gamma(2.000) = 2.000, z = 0),
      the deep-window lock gamma(1.20) = 2.667 sits ON the measured MW outer
      slope (z = -0.92),
      and the cluster lock gamma(3.16) = 1.633 sits ON the measured cluster inner
      (z = -0.41) and
      residual (z = -0.62).
      B and C are excluded by the phantom point at >= 16.7 sigma (sigma_eff 0.02)
      and score the galaxy-scale pair on the wrong side (dust z_B +3.14 / z_C +3.65
      vs z_A -1.91).  The n-window channels do NOT discriminate alone (all three
      conventions put the cluster locks on the measured cluster slopes) -- the
      phantom closure is the discriminator, as it must be for an off-by-one at n = 2.
  V3  THE HONEST STATEMENT: THE REVERSE LOCK SURVIVES, CORRECTED-AND-HOLDING --
      the committed formula gamma = (2+n)/n (H055) IS the corrected one; the
      off-by-one suspicion is settled WITH THE NUMBER (the phantom identity and
      the MW interior gamma = 2.000 exact, z_A = 0 / z_B = -16.7 / z_C = -25 at
      the realized sigma).  THE FORWARD CHAIN (H060) IS UNAFFECTED: it was always
      verified forward only (deep limit 2u -> g^2 = a0 g_N -> rho ~ r^-2 -> M ~ r)
      and never used the reverse step.  G229's PARTIALLY-CONFIRMED is re-scored
      UPWARD at its anchor: the one clean one-component point -- the phantom
      n = 2 <-> gamma = 2.000 EXACT realized in the MW interior (G072/G188) -- is
      the adjudicated core and is now CLOSED; the PARTIAL status survives only
      through the WEDGE IN n (G158 deep-end 1.20 vs G183 reconciled 3.16), which
      is a dispute about which n the windows select, NOT about the lock relation.
      The reverse direction is NOT dead: it lives, formula unchanged, anchor exact.
  REGISTERED: G230's direct composite dM/dg FAILED its own V1 (pooled p = 3.47 +- 0.20,
      z = +7.3 vs -2) -- the lock is NOT re-confirmed by the composite dM/dg; the
      per-halo g^-2 face is the kinematic identity |dM/dg| = v_flat^4/(G g^2) of any
      near-flat curve; the adjudicating measurement is the MW-inner phantom slope.

